From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:34:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] T-505 item 4: the CPU band frames the GPU path's default
 (JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=0 turns them off)

The band frames composed on the CPU from the tiles (the fork's 88a1b3eaaf) were behind
JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=1. The cavekit Deciding Vote of 2026-11-04 (Codex, on the rounds' numbers:
the long page's band frame 22.0 -> 4.7 ms on the compositor thread, the express frames made in
14 ms median against 31, the worst lag 294 -> 131 ms, the verify 0 wrong of 121; the resolution
switch a loss on Wikipedia) picked them as the default with the daemon's resolution switch off
and no scaler. So JihadCpuBandsWanted() and the tile read lock kept after the immediate upload
(TextureHost.cpp) now follow JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR, as the pull mode and the direct path do,
unless JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=0. The memory rounds of the same day measured the kept locks'
double-buffering (docs/rounds/finger-2026-11-04/notes.txt, "The default").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp      | 6 ++++--
 gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp b/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
index 0755f806d8..b143d8285a 100644
--- a/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
@@ -847,12 +847,14 @@ BufferTextureHost::MaybeUpload(nsIntRegion *aRegion)
   if (mHasIntermediateBuffer) {
     // We just did the texture upload, the content side can now freely write
     // into the shared buffer.
-    // Jihad T-505 item 4 (JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=1): not while the band frames are composed on the CPU from these
+    // Jihad T-505 item 4 (the GPU path's default; JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=0 turns it off): not while the band frames
+    // are composed on the CPU from these
     // buffers (CompositorBridgeParent's JihadCpuBands reads them under the tile host): the content side would
     // paint the tile's next content into the same front buffer (TileClient::GetBackBuffer reuses an unlocked
     // front buffer) while the compositor thread copies it. The lock stays until the tile is dropped
     // (UnbindTextureSource, or the host's end); the content side double-buffers the tile meanwhile.
-    static const bool sJihadKeep = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS") && atoi(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS")) != 0;
+    static const bool sJihadKeep = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR") != nullptr &&
+                                   !(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS") && atoi(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS")) == 0);
     if (!sJihadKeep) ReadUnlock();
   }
 
diff --git a/gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp b/gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp
index 62f7153bf3..5539b7f61c 100644
--- a/gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp
@@ -1564,7 +1564,8 @@ JihadFixedCols()
   return sOn && !sJihadContentOnly;   // T-505: a frame without its parts has no fixed pixels to keep or read
 }
 
-// T-505 item 4 (2026-11-04): the band frames composed on the CPU from the tiles. JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=1: a band frame
+// T-505 item 4 (2026-11-04): the band frames composed on the CPU from the tiles — the GPU path's default (the
+// Deciding Vote of 2026-11-04, Codex, on the rounds' numbers; JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=0 turns it off): a band frame
 // (a scroll-only frame, or one whose change fits the band pass) whose band rows are covered by tiled painted layers
 // and colour layers only — each drawn "over" at full opacity, no mask, under a translation of whole frame pixels at
 // a scale of 1 (the layers painted at the card's zoom's resolution: the daemon's JIHAD_GPU_RES_ZOOM) — is composed
@@ -1581,7 +1582,8 @@ JihadFixedCols()
 static bool
 JihadCpuBandsWanted()
 {
-  static const bool sOn = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS") && atoi(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS")) != 0;
+  static const bool sOn = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR") != nullptr &&
+                          !(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS") && atoi(getenv("JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS")) == 0);
   return sOn;
 }
 
@@ -2731,7 +2733,7 @@ CompositorBridgeParent::JihadComposeAndRead(JihadFrameRequest* aReq, float aScal
       // JihadSetRegions); JIHAD_GPU_PASS_PER_REGION=1 composes each on its own, as before
       static const bool sPassPerRegion = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_PASS_PER_REGION") != nullptr;
       // T-505 item 4: the bands composed on the CPU from the tiles when every layer under them allows it
-      // (JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=1, JihadCpuBands above: a frame of full-width bands alone, no column chunks); the GPU
+      // (the GPU path's default, JihadCpuBands above: a frame of full-width bands alone, no column chunks); the GPU
       // band pass otherwise, as before
       bool cpuDone = false;
       double msCpuPrep = 0, msCpuDraw = 0;
